    "narrative": "The cornerstone of our lineup today is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who sits comfortably atop our daily board with a 79.71 efficiency score. Facing Montero, K., **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a high-leverage batting order position (#2) and a favorable opposing xERA of 4.51, making him our primary engine for counting stats. **Will Smith** (65.60) also presents a high-floor start, capitalizing on a weak matchup against Canning and a strong xwOBA profile. While the remainder of our core\u2014including **Luis Arraez** (61.05), **Daulton Varsho** (60.63), and **Matt Chapman** (59.61)\u2014all clear the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, they rely heavily on favorable platoon splits to overcome mediocre SP matchups. **Bryson Stott** and **Jonathan Aranda** find themselves in tougher spots against Burns, Ch. and Bradish respectively; while their platoon advantages keep them relevant, their ceiling is dampened by the high-caliber arms they are forced to confront.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Taylor Ward** on the bench. With a score of 39.38, he missed our \"marginal\" floor by less than a point. While his leadoff status provides a situational boost, the optimizer penalized his projected production due to a negative park factor and an unfavorable matchup against Jax. Consequently, he remains a spectator to preserve our game caps. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Lawrence Butler** and **Tyler Freeman** are currently absent from their respective lineups, offering zero utility for today\u2019s 5x5 rotation. Owners should watch the wind and weather reports closely for the **Gavin Sheets** start; his 41.89 score is precarious, and any late-breaking atmospheric changes could quickly push him below our replacement-level threshold.",
